.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-snapshot 1  "tapectl-snapshot " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-snapshot \- Manage snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl snapshot\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage snapshots
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tapectl\-snapshot\-create(1)
Create a snapshot (fast directory walk + manifest)
.TP
tapectl\-snapshot\-list(1)
List snapshots
.TP
tapectl\-snapshot\-diff(1)
Compare two snapshot versions of a unit
.TP
tapectl\-snapshot\-delete(1)
Delete an unwritten snapshot
.TP
tapectl\-snapshot\-purge(1)
Purge a reclaimable snapshot (remove DB records)
.TP
tapectl\-snapshot\-mark\-reclaimable(1)
Mark a snapshot as reclaimable (with enforced preconditions)
.TP
tapectl\-snapshot\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
